    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0542" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2630</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-05T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1916, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2975. Please telegraph me what use, if any, has been made of memorandum quoted in
                    my 2951, April 28, and whether it was made known to the German Government before
                    the dispatch of its note on submarine warfare which you are now forwarding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
